 apparel, applicators, bags and bulk bags, bottles and vials, building materials, canisters and jerrycans, drinking cups, films and laminates, jars, lids, tapes and adhesives, trays, tubes, wipes packaging solutions, and miscellaneous and accessories, as well as tubs and pots. The company's Global Flexible Packaging Solutions segment develops and supplies flexible packaging; and supplies polymer resin, aluminum, and fiber based flexible packaging solutions. Its Global Rigid Packaging Solutions segment manufactures rigid packaging containers, closures, dispensing and pharma delivery devices, and related products. The company sells its products through its direct sales force. Amcor plc was incorporated in 1926 and is headquartered in Zurich, Switzerland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Peter  Konieczny Dip Eng, MBA, MSc Mech Eng | CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $3.7M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 75K people. Revenue per employee of $313K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 14%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $16K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Amcor plc is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $20.7B market cap on $23.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 20% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $1.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.94\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 25% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Amcor (AMCR) Stock May Be 48% Undervalued Following Dividend Raise","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-amcr/amcor/news/amcor-amcr-stock-may-be-48-undervalued-following-dividend-ra","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794003726.716,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.863,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Amcor PLC $AMCR Shares Newly Acquired by Mirae Asset Global Investments Co. Ltd.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/amcor-plc-amcr-shares-newly-acquired-by-mirae-asset-global-investments-co-ltd.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793959564.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.944,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Amcor (AMCR) Tests Its Valuation After Higher Dividend And Lower EPS Outlook","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/amcor-amcr-tests-valuation-higher-032255310.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793935375.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.872,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance","dividend"]},{"title":"Is Amcor (AMCR) Still Undervalued As Sales Beat But EPS Guidance Was Trimmed?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-amcr/amcor/news/is-amcor-amcr-still-undervalued-as-sales-beat-but-eps-guidan","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793913997.134,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.984,"tier":0,"scope":"comp