ore of 7/9 and cash conversion of 1.94x.","ROE of 9% is amplified by 3.1x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 0.7% of revenue on R&D and 0.4% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.8x net debt to EBITDA ($1.1B of cash against $14.0B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 2.8x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.37 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD.","The Beneish M-score (-2.15) sits just under the manipulation line, so earnings quality bears watching."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 17.0% over 3 years and 12.8% over 5 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 20%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 4.4% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (3.9% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 18, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","Analysts expect 7.7% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and institutions hold 79%.","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 1 sale over the past year, net $972K bought.","It returns 5.7% a year to shareholders (5.9% in dividends).","It pays out 112% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["With about 75,000 employees, each generates about $313K of revenue, 0.8x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 13.9% a year.","That works out to $16K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.7M (12x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $1K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":59,"head":"Invest: trades 25% below fair value of $60.22; revenue grew 12.8%/yr over 5y.","pros":["Model rating LEA